Introduction
------------

This README describes the layout, structure, and means to maintain the
tests_mock subdirectory tree.

tests_mock serves to parallel the tests directory tree, with matching of
*.py path names and within each file, tests, for those tests that do not
require physical hardware GPUs. Each test that appears in a test_*.py either
"trampolines" to an existing test with the same name in a file in the same
sub-path under tests, that does not require live GPUs, or calls a "helper"
function in such a file that is also called with a similar test in the target
file, but with different decorators -- the decorators distinguishing between
using live GPUs in the one case, and NVML-injected fake GPUs in the other.

Example
-------

This is an excerpt from tests_mock/test_action.py:

from tests.test_action import helper_dcgm_action_validate_embedded
from tests.test_action import helper_dcgm_action_validate_remote
from tests.test_action import helper_dcgm_action_run_diag_embedded
from tests.test_action import helper_dcgm_action_run_diag_remote
from tests.test_action import helper_dcgm_action_run_diag_gpu_list
from tests.test_action import helper_dcgm_action_run_diag_bad_validation

from _test_helpers import skip_test_if_no_dcgm_nvml

import test_utils
# Explicit so trampoline introspection works.
from test_utils import trampoline


@test_utils.run_with_injection_nvml_using_specific_sku('A100.yaml')
@test_utils.run_with_embedded_host_engine()
@test_utils.run_with_nvml_injected_gpus()
@test_utils.for_all_same_sku_gpus()
@test_utils.run_only_as_root()
@test_utils.run_with_max_power_limit_set()
def test_dcgm_action_validate_embedded(handle, gpuIds):
    helper_dcgm_action_validate_embedded(handle, gpuIds)

...

def test_dcgm_action_run_diag_on_heterogeneous_env():
    trampoline()

Here, we import the helper functions used by GPU-centric tests in
tests/test_action.py and GPU-less tests in tests_mock/test_action.py. The
test test_dcgm_action_validate_embedded in tests/test_action likely uses live
GPUs, but we substitute an NVML-injected A100 GPU using the A100.yaml. The
difference is managed by different decorator sequences. Refactoring a test
under tests into a helper and a decorated test that calls it is a common
process.

The test test_dcgm_action_run_diag_on_heterogeneous_env calls an existing
test in tests/test_action.py with the same name, using its decorators. This
is expected to be an existing (legacy, if you will) test that does not require
live GPUs.

trampoline() is not usually executed (though it would run the similar test
under tests, if run) -- it is processed by the test framework using
introspection to identfy the test to run.

This is achieved by explicitly importing trampoline from test_utils.

Running tests under tests_mock instead of tests
-----------------------------------------------

Running main.py accepts --test-dirs to specify test directory roots other than
the default tests (and multiple directories can be specified, separated by
commas, so tests and tests_mock tests can be run as a single pass, with
duplicates run only once). Alternately, specifying --no-hw (no hardware)
appends _mock to all test directories specified with --test-dirs (with tests as
the default, so tests_mock), will run the mocked test suite as opposed to the
live and legacy non-hardware test suite.

Reporting on Hardware-only, non-Hardware, and Mocked-Hardware
-------------------------------------------------------------

A script has been included in testing/python3, test_state.py which, if run from
that directory will compare tests in tests_mock and tests and report which ones
are Hardware-only, non-Hardware, and Mocked-Hardware. If run on a HEAD of
a branch and prior to a commit, and diffing the results, tests can be identified
that might be considered for mocking.
